      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>What interconnect methods does Hana offer?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Hana provides wire bond, flip chip and GGI (gold-to-gold interconnect) bonding at chip level, together with ACF (anisotropic conductive film) and hot-bar bonding for flex, display and module interconnect, including flex-to-PCB and flex-to-ceramic.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>How do you decide which method to use?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">The method is selected according to the device’s electrical, mechanical, geometry and reliability requirements. Supporting multiple interconnect technologies allows the process to be matched to the application.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>How are interconnects verified?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Verification includes pull and shear testing to MIL-STD-883 methods, X-ray on bump and joint arrays, and post-bond AOI, with per-unit traceability.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Can you mix methods on one assembly?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. Wire bond, flip chip, GGI and film bonding can be combined within a single assembly where required by the product design.</div>
    </details>
